  "raw": {
    "https://www.fau.edu/about/faculty-staff/": {
      "title": "Faculty & Staff",
      "description": "Faculty and Staff | Florida Atlantic University Skip to main content FLORIDA ATLANTIC UNIVERSITY students faculty/staff alumni families apply visit give admissions academics research campus life athletics Faculty & Staff QUICK LINKS Workday Canvas MYFAU IT Helpdesk Directory Facilities Request Parking LinkedIn Learning Resources Academic Calendar Course Schedule Emergency FAU Police Human Resources Libraries Photo Database Order Promotional Items Visual Standards Florida Atlantic University 777 Glades Road Boca Raton, FL 33431 Campuses Boca Raton Dania Beach Davie Fort Lauderdale Harbor Branch Jupiter Resources Academic Calendar Employment Opportunities Program Search Parking Report a Concern Transcripts Info Contact Us Directory Emergency & Safety FAU Schools Media Social facebook twitter youtube instagram linkedin Search Programs Request Info Visit Our Campuses If you are experiencing difficulty accessing information on the Florida Atlantic University website due to a disability, visit the website accessibility page. Florida Atlantic University embodies a culture of strategic and collaborative community engagement that results in mutual benefit to the institution and the internal and external communities that it serves. Privacy Policy Regulations & Policies Consumer Information Get Help Site Index Student Accessibility Public Records 2026 Florida Atlantic University ©"
    },
    "https://www.fau.edu/jobs/": {
      "title": "Innovation & Unbridled Ambition",
      "description": "FAU JOBS | Florida Atlantic University Skip to main content FLORIDA ATLANTIC UNIVERSITY students faculty/staff alumni families apply visit give FAU Home FAU JOBS MENU HOME Home PEOPLE People LIFE AT FAU Life at FAU EXPLORE SOUTH FLORIDA Explore South Florida APPLICANT RESOURCES Applicant Resources APPLY NOW Apply Now FAU JOBS FAU is Where Your Future Begins Join us on our journey in pushing the boundaries of higher education Explore Jobs at FAU Innovation & Unbridled Ambition We have over 30,000 students from all 50 states and over 180 countries, 21 intercollegiate teams, 180 plus degree programs, and an administration that thrives on discovery and excellence. Florida Atlantic’s faculty and staff are trailblazers and innovators with a passion for finding creative solutions while advancing science, art, and technology in all disciplines. Our work environment is a hub of cultures from across the nation and the world, making FAU a place where collaboration flourishes. Student success, excellence, and community engagement are some of our highest values as a university. These values are prominent throughout FAU’s community and are essential to the employee experience. To learn about the vision and mission of FAU, please visit: www.fau.edu Benefits & Wellness At FAU we care about you at work and at home. This is why we put work-life balance at the forefront for our employees. From competitive health benefits and retirement options to employee discounts, state of the art fitness centers and on campus family care options, FAU makes your transition from home to work as smooth as possible. Read more about the benefits we have to offer. Benefits Guide 2023/24 Education We are a place where employees can become students and students can become employees. Our Employee Educational Scholarship Program (EESP) provides employees with the opportunity to continue their educational goals at FAU. Employees who qualify for this program can take up to six credit hours for free per semester. Read more about education opportunities for employees at FAU. Time Off Refresh, find an adventure, or just enjoy some well-earned you time. We understand the importance of taking time for yourself, which is why we have generous time off options available. This includes major holidays, winter break, earned time off, a personal holiday and even a volunteer day to use for a cause you care about. Taking care of yourself is important, especially when you are under the weather. At FAU, you will have the opportunity to take the time you need to recover with our competitive sick leave policy. Learn more about our time off options. Connect with FAU HR facebook instagram “From SeaTech in Ft. Lauderdale to Harbor Branch in Ft. Pierce, FAU’s services stretch over 100 miles. I think this sets us apart from any other university.” Dr. Ali Zilouchian Professor, Computer and Electrical Engineering Florida Atlantic University 777 Glades Road Boca Raton, FL 33431 Campuses Boca Raton Dania Beach Davie Fort Lauderdale Harbor Branch Jupiter Resources Academic Calendar Employment Opportunities Program Search Parking Report a Concern Transcripts Info Contact Us Directory Emergency & Safety FAU Schools Media Social facebook twitter youtube instagram linkedin Search Programs Request Info Visit Our Campuses If you are experiencing difficulty accessing information on the Florida Atlantic University website due to a disability, visit the website accessibility page. Florida Atlantic University embodies a culture of strategic and collaborative community engagement that results in mutual benefit to the institution and the internal and external communities that it serves. Privacy Policy Regulations & Policies Consumer Information Get Help Site Index Student Accessibility Public Records 2026 Florida Atlantic University ©"
    },
    "https://www.fau.edu/jobs/people/": {
      "title": "People",
      "description": "FAU JOBS - PEOPLE | Florida Atlantic University Skip to main content FLORIDA ATLANTIC UNIVERSITY students faculty/staff alumni families apply visit give FAU Home FAU JOBS FAU JOBS- PEOPLE MENU HOME Home PEOPLE People LIFE AT FAU Life at FAU EXPLORE SOUTH FLORIDA Explore South Florida APPLICANT RESOURCES Applicant Resources APPLY NOW Apply Now FAU JOBS People Captain Larry Ervin Law Enforcement Captain \"It’s a beautiful day! Why not sing?\" For Captain Larry Ervin, bringing a smile to the faces of those he encounters at FAU is just as important as making sure they are safe and comfortable on campus. He is known for breaking out in song throughout the day, and his voice brightens up every building, office, and walkway he steps into. \"We’re interactive in our community. That’s what we’re about.\" To Captain Ervin, the FAU community is his family. \"People are always telling me, ‘It’s 50,000 people here,’ but I still think it’s 50,000 family members.\" As the FAU family continues to grow, Captain Ervin feels that his greatest accomplishment has been creating a safe environment where students can feel comfortable any time they are on campus. He also greatly admires the diversity within FAU’s community as it provides an opportunity for Owls to learn more about the world and embrace other cultures. \"When you’re walking down that breezeway, and you look up and down, you see there are different types of cultures, and that is great.\" DR. FRANCISCO PRESUEL-MORENO Associate Professor To Dr. Presuel-Moreno, Associate Professor of Ocean and Mechanical Engineering, \"being an Owl means being more than just being someone who teaches a class. It means being someone who students can relate to. It means being a resource for them.\" Dr. Presuel-Moreno, who is a two time recipient of the Researcher of the Year award, teaches engineering courses at FAU’s SeaTech campus, which is located right on the coast of Dania Beach. SeaTech’s stunning beachfront location is a major benefit for the research that he and his colleagues conduct because it provides invaluable accessibility to the ocean. Faculty and students utilizing the University’s research boats are able to reach the open ocean in under ten minutes. In addition to the University’s location, Dr. Presuel-Moreno feels that FAU provides extensive resources to assist in furthering his knowledge and academic prestige. Some of these resources include benefits that the University offers, such as its healthcare and retirement plans, which make it easier for faculty like Dr. Presuel-Moreno to focus on their students and research. Another facet of the University that Dr. Presuel-Moreno values is its strong diversity. The ocean engineering program attracts people from all over the nation, so it results in, as he says, \"a great collage of people.\" And he finds it very rewarding to see the growth of those students throughout the program. \"You see the progression from the first day to when they graduate. You see how they mature, and you get a chance to see how they have grown during their time here at FAU.\" Florida Atlantic University 777 Glades Road Boca Raton, FL 33431 Campuses Boca Raton Dania Beach Davie Fort Lauderdale Harbor Branch Jupiter Resources Academic Calendar Employment Opportunities Program Search Parking Report a Concern Transcripts Info Contact Us Directory Emergency & Safety FAU Schools Media Social facebook twitter youtube instagram linkedin Search Programs Request Info Visit Our Campuses If you are experiencing difficulty accessing information on the Florida Atlantic University website due to a disability, visit the website accessibility page. Florida Atlantic University embodies a culture of strategic and collaborative community engagement that results in mutual benefit to the institution and the internal and external communities that it serves. Privacy Policy Regulations & Policies Consumer Information Get Help Site Index Student Accessibility Public Records 2026 Florida Atlantic University ©"
    },
    "https://www.fau.edu/jobs/fau-life/": {
      "title": "FAU. Enjoy Where You Work",
      "description": "FAU JOBS | Florida Atlantic University Skip to main content FLORIDA ATLANTIC UNIVERSITY students faculty/staff alumni families apply visit give FAU Home FAU JOBS FAU JOBS MENU HOME Home PEOPLE People LIFE AT FAU Life at FAU EXPLORE SOUTH FLORIDA Explore South Florida APPLICANT RESOURCES Applicant Resources APPLY NOW Apply Now FAU JOBS FAU is Where Your Future Begins Join us on our journey in pushing the boundaries of higher education Explore Jobs at FAU FAU. Enjoy Where You Work Dining When hunger strikes, there’s no need to worry because FAU has a variety of dining options available. Campus dining options include Starbucks, Dunkin’ Donuts, Papa John’s, Chick-fil-a, Subway, FAU’s own on-campus restaurant, Burrow Bar & Grill, and more! To see all of FAU’s dining options, please visit FAU Dining Services. Fitness From yoga and running trails to rock climbing and challenge courses, FAU offers a multitude of options to stay fit, including our own state of the art fitness center at Campus Recreation. For more information, please visit Campus Recreation. Sports & Entertainment Working at FAU means getting to enjoy the many events and activities on campus such as catching a movie at the Living Room Theaters, cheering on the Owls at one of the many sporting events, attending a guest speaker event, and more. For more information, view FAU’s Calendar of Events Family Care FAU has education and family care options available, so your family is never too far away. FAU’s family care options include: Karen Slattery Educational Research Center for Child Development for infants to VPK, A.D. Henderson University School and FAU High School for K - 12 students, and the Adult Day Center at the Louis and Anne Green Memory and Wellness Center. Our Campuses Boca Raton Dania Beach Davie Fort Lauderdale Harbor Branch Jupiter BOCA RATON 777 Glades Road Boca Raton, FL 33431 Florida Atlantic University was founded in 1964 in Boca Raton on an 850-acre site located near the Atlantic Ocean. The campus is conveniently located half way between Palm Beach and Fort Lauderdale and offers a broad range of academic programs, activities, and services. The Boca Raton Campus provides an exciting and supportive learning environment for students. The Student Union hosts student activities and meetings. In addition, its 2,400-seat Carole and Barry Kaye Performing Arts Auditorium enables students to enjoy performances ranging from rock groups to the Florida Philharmonic Orchestra. The campus supports two cafeterias and has an attractive array of accommodations for its residential students. The Boca Raton Campus is also the home of FAU's Division I Intercollegiate Athletics program and facilities. Its recreation complex includes an aquatic center, gymnasium, tennis courts, wellness center, track, and a variety of fields for club and intramural sports competition. DANIA BEACH 101 North Beach Road Dania Beach, FL 33004 The Dania Beach facility is home to ocean engineering research and technology development in the areas of acoustics, marine vehicles, hydrodynamics and physical oceanography, marine materials and nanocomposites. Dania Beach builds on five decades of excellence at FAU as home to one of the nation's first ocean engineering programs. DAVIE 3200 College Avenue Davie, FL 33314 More than 5,000 students take classes at FAU's second-largest campus. Conveniently located (central Broward County) with Broward College as part of the South Florida Education Center, FAU Davie offers coursework in 30 degree programs through the colleges of Arts and Letters, Business, Design and Social Inquiry, Nursing, and Science. The campus features more than 300,000 square feet of labs, classrooms and faculty, staff and student offices. It also hosts the innovative Teaching and Leadership Center and is the base of operations for FAU's Everglades research and restoration efforts. FORT LAUDERDALE 111 East Las Olas Blvd. Fort Lauderdale, FL 33301 Located in downtown Fort Lauderdale, the campus provides a \"real life\" urban laboratory for students pursuing an accredited degree in architecture and is the location for the College of Business' Executive Master of Accounting program. The campus also is home to MetroLab, a collaborative exhibition and event space for FAU's engagement with the community. HARBOR BRANCH 5600 US 1 North Fort Pierce, FL 34946 FAU's Harbor Branch Oceanographic Institute (HBOI) is dedicated to exploring the world's oceans and integrating the science and technology of the sea with the needs of humankind. As a base of operations for a host of research and academic programs -- such as coral reef and estuary studies, marine mammal rescue and rehabilitation, semester-at-sea programs and a variety of research positions and internships -- undergraduate students, graduate students and faculty find HBOI's high-tech facilities and dynamic environment perfect for their varied pursuits. JUPITER 5600 US 1 North Fort Pierce, FL 34946 FAU's Harbor Branch Oceanographic Institute (HBOI) is dedicated to exploring the world's oceans and integrating the science and technology of the sea with the needs of humankind. As a base of operations for a host of research and academic programs -- such as coral reef and estuary studies, marine mammal rescue and rehabilitation, semester-at-sea programs and a variety of research positions and internships -- undergraduate students, graduate students and faculty find HBOI's high-tech facilities and dynamic environment perfect for their varied pursuits. Florida Atlantic University 777 Glades Road Boca Raton, FL 33431 Campuses Boca Raton Dania Beach Davie Fort Lauderdale Harbor Branch Jupiter Resources Academic Calendar Employment Opportunities Program Search Parking Report a Concern Transcripts Info Contact Us Directory Emergency & Safety FAU Schools Media Social facebook twitter youtube instagram linkedin Search Programs Request Info Visit Our Campuses If you are experiencing difficulty accessing information on the Florida Atlantic University website due to a disability, visit the website accessibility page. Florida Atlantic University embodies a culture of strategic and collaborative community engagement that results in mutual benefit to the institution and the internal and external communities that it serves. Privacy Policy Regulations & Policies Consumer Information Get Help Site Index Student Accessibility Public Records 2026 Florida Atlantic University ©"
    },
    "https://www.fau.edu/jobs/explore/": {
      "title": "WHY NOT LIVE WHERE EVERYONE VACATIONS?",
      "description": "EXPLORE SOUTH FLORIDA | Florida Atlantic University Skip to main content FLORIDA ATLANTIC UNIVERSITY students faculty/staff alumni families apply visit give FAU Home FAU JOBS EXPLORE SOUTH FLORIDA MENU HOME Home PEOPLE People LIFE AT FAU Life at FAU EXPLORE SOUTH FLORIDA Explore South Florida APPLICANT RESOURCES Applicant Resources APPLY NOW Apply Now FAU JOBS WHY NOT LIVE WHERE EVERYONE VACATIONS? Florida Atlantic University is located in the paradise that is South Florida with campuses that stretch along Florida's coast between America’s Everglades and the Atlantic Ocean. 231 days of sunshine, golden beaches, and an incredibly diverse population make South Florida an eclectic tropical destination. It is a destination where you can choose your own adventure, whether it's enjoying the tranquility of the crystal clear waters, exploring the vibrant shops, or experiencing the exciting nightlife and unparalleled restaurants. South Florida is also the home of the conference-winning Florida Panthers and the championship-winning Miami Heat, Marlins, and Dolphins. Attending a game is a must-have experience. Weekend getaways are easy when living in South Florida. With Miami, the Florida Keys, the Gulf Coast and Orlando a short drive away and the Caribbean Islands a short flight or cruise away, South Florida has it all. See what makes the counties Florida Atlantic serves great places to live, work, and play. PALM BEACH COUNTY 47 miles of Atlantic coastline, one of a kind state parks, and stylish places to live, shop, and explore. Palm Beach County is home to FAU's Boca and Jupiter campuses. Fun things in the area include: Gumbo Limbo Environmental Center Jupiter Lighthouse Palm Beach Zoo CityPlace Peanut Island Roger Dean Stadium Morikami Museum Rapids Water Park Palm Beach Outlets Arthur R. Marshall Loxahatchee National Wildlife Refuge Lion Country Safari Broward County Framed by bright blue beaches and the exotic Everglades, Broward County is a place of endless opportunities. Broward County is home to FAU's Davie, Dania Beach, and Ft. Lauderdale campuses. Fun things in the area include: Las Olas Boulevard Everglades Holiday Park Broward Center for the Performing Arts Museum of Discovery and Science Butterfly World Quiet Waters Park FATVillage Art Walks Sawgrass Outlets International Swimming Hall of Fame C.B. Smith Park Intracoastal Waterway Tours St. Lucie County Dynamic, historic cities, and breathtaking beaches make St. Lucie County a great home to FAU's Harbor Branch Oceanographic Institute in Fort Pierce. Fun things in the area include: Navy Seal Museum St. Lucie County Aquarium Heathcote Botanical Gardens Manatee Observation & Education Center Savannas Preserve State Park A.E. Backus Gallery & Museum Tradition Field Oxbow Eco-Center Walton Rocks Beach and Dog Park Riverwalk Boardwalk Sunrise Theatre for the Performing Arts Florida Atlantic University 777 Glades Road Boca Raton, FL 33431 Campuses Boca Raton Dania Beach Davie Fort Lauderdale Harbor Branch Jupiter Resources Academic Calendar Employment Opportunities Program Search Parking Report a Concern Transcripts Info Contact Us Directory Emergency & Safety FAU Schools Media Social facebook twitter youtube instagram linkedin Search Programs Request Info Visit Our Campuses If you are experiencing difficulty accessing information on the Florida Atlantic University website due to a disability, visit the website accessibility page. Florida Atlantic University embodies a culture of strategic and collaborative community engagement that results in mutual benefit to the institution and the internal and external communities that it serves. Privacy Policy Regulations & Policies Consumer Information Get Help Site Index Student Accessibility Public Records 2026 Florida Atlantic University ©"
    },
    "https://www.fau.edu/jobs/resources/": {
      "title": "APPLICANT RESOURCES",
      "description": "APPLICANT RESOURCES | Florida Atlantic University Skip to main content FLORIDA ATLANTIC UNIVERSITY students faculty/staff alumni families apply visit give FAU Home FAU JOBS APPLICANT RESOURCES MENU HOME Home PEOPLE People LIFE AT FAU Life at FAU EXPLORE SOUTH FLORIDA Explore South Florida APPLICANT RESOURCES Applicant Resources APPLY NOW Apply Now FAU JOBS SUB MENU FAU JOBS Applicant Resources Veterans' Preference Job Categories FAQS APPLICANT RESOURCES FAU provides an environment where creativeness is cultivated, and inventiveness is encouraged. Our faculty and staff make up a diverse community of contemporary thinkers, achievers and explorers. This distinct and innovative work environment provides opportunities available for all experience levels. We thank you for your interest in joining FAU on its race to excellence. In order to be considered for a position, you must apply through our career site. Applicant Tutorials For instructions on how to apply through our new applicant portal, please review the applicable tutorial below. Each tutorial provides step-by-step instructions on how to successfully submit an application. Internal Applicant Tutorial (Current FAU Employees) This section is for current Florida Atlantic University employees applying for internal job opportunities. Accessing Internal Job Postings 1. Log in to Workday at: https://workday.fau.edu 2. Access internal postings by: Selecting the Career worklet and choosing Find Internal Jobs – FAU, or Searching for Find Internal Jobs – FAU using the Workday search bar. 3. Select a position to review requirements and qualifications. Applying for a Position 1. Select Apply from the job posting. 2. Complete each section of the application, ensuring all required fields are filled. 3. Application requirements vary by position type: AMP and Faculty positions: Resume and cover letter are required. SP, OPS, and Student positions: Completion of the Job History section is required. Updating Job History (if needed) 1. Select Go to your profile within the application. 2. Navigate to Job > Professional Profile in Workday. 3. Add or upload experience as needed. 4. Return to your Workday Inbox to continue the application. Final Review and Submission Verify all information and attachments. Review the Special Instructions section for any additional required documents. Select Submit to complete your application. You may also choose Save for Later if you need to return at a later time. External Applicant Tutorial (Non‑FAU Employees) This section is for individuals who are not currently employed by Florida Atlantic University and are applying for positions through FAU’s public careers site. Accessing the FAU Careers Site 1. Navigate to the FAU applicant portal: https://fau.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/FAU 2. Browse available positions by scrolling the page or using the search function. 3. Select a position to view details, qualifications, and Special Instructions to Applicants. Creating or Accessing an Applicant Account New applicants must create an account to apply. Returning applicants should sign in using their existing credentials. Do not create multiple applicant accounts. If you cannot remember your password, use the Forgot Password feature. Completing the Application 1. Select Apply or Apply with LinkedIn, if available. 2. Follow the on‑screen instructions to complete each section of the application. 3. Fields marked with an asterisk (*) are required. 4. You may use resume parsing or copy‑and‑paste text, but retype special characters (such as apostrophes or accent marks) to avoid system issues. Uploading Required Documents Review the Special Instructions to Applicants section carefully to determine required attachments. Common required documents may include: Resume Cover letter DD‑214 (for Veterans’ Preference, if applicable) You can upload documents during the application process and review them before submitting. Reviewing and Submitting Review all information entered before submitting. Use the Back button to correct any section. Click Submit to complete your application. A confirmation message will display once your application is successfully received. Attaching Documents to an Application This section applies to both internal and external applicants. Before You Begin Always review the Special Instructions to Applicants in the job posting to confirm: Which documents are required Whether multiple documents must be uploaded separately Uploading Documents Using Quick Apply If you choose Quick Apply, one document (usually your resume) may upload automatically. To add additional documents: Use the Upload option in the Resume/CV section. Repeat until all required documents are attached. Uploading Documents Without Quick Apply 1. Navigate to the Resume/CV section during the application. 2. Upload documents by: Dragging and dropping files, or Selecting files manually. 3. Once one document is uploaded, you may upload additional files as needed. Final Review Confirm all required documents are attached. Use the Back button to make corrections if needed. Submit the application once all materials are complete. Updating Email Address and Contact Information Applicants may update their contact details after an application has been submitted. Updating Your Email Address 1. Log in to your applicant account. 2. Access Account Settings. 3. Enter a new email address and submit the update. 4. Check your email for a verification message and follow the link provided. 5. Log in using your updated email address once verification is complete. Updating Contact Information Applicants may update: Name Address Phone number To do so: 1. Log in to your applicant account. 2. Navigate to your profile and select Update Contact Information. 3. Make updates as necessary and save changes. If you have any questions regarding the application process, please email jobs@fau.edu or 561-297-3057. Additional Information Florida Atlantic University is an equal opportunity/equal access institution and all qualified applicants will receive consideration without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability status, protected veterans status or other protected status. Individuals with disabilities requiring accommodation, please call 561-297-3058. 711 connects you to a 24/7 Telecommunications Relay Service (TRS). For any questions, please contact FAU Recruitment Service at jobs@fau.edu . Florida Atlantic University 777 Glades Road Boca Raton, FL 33431 Campuses Boca Raton Dania Beach Davie Fort Lauderdale Harbor Branch Jupiter Resources Academic Calendar Employment Opportunities Program Search Parking Report a Concern Transcripts Info Contact Us Directory Emergency & Safety FAU Schools Media Social facebook twitter youtube instagram linkedin Search Programs Request Info Visit Our Campuses If you are experiencing difficulty accessing information on the Florida Atlantic University website due to a disability, visit the website accessibility page. Florida Atlantic University embodies a culture of strategic and collaborative community engagement that results in mutual benefit to the institution and the internal and external communities that it serves. Privacy Policy Regulations & Policies Consumer Information Get Help Site Index Student Accessibility Public Records 2026 Florida Atlantic University ©"
    },
    "https://www.fau.edu/jobs/apply/": {
      "title": "THANK YOU FOR YOUR INTEREST IN EMPLOYMENT AT FAU",
      "description": "THANK YOU FOR YOUR INTEREST IN EMPLOYMENT AT FAU | Florida Atlantic University Skip to main content FLORIDA ATLANTIC UNIVERSITY students faculty/staff alumni families apply visit give FAU Home FAU JOBS THANK YOU FOR YOUR INTEREST IN EMPLOYMENT AT FAU MENU HOME Home PEOPLE People LIFE AT FAU Life at FAU EXPLORE SOUTH FLORIDA Explore South Florida APPLICANT RESOURCES Applicant Resources APPLY NOW Apply Now FAU JOBS THANK YOU FOR YOUR INTEREST IN EMPLOYMENT AT FAU Application for employment must be submitted through our career site. To apply or check the status of a position, follow the appropriate instructions below: Prospective Applicants (Non-FAU employees) External applicants (non-FAU employee) will need to visit our new applicant portal . First-time applicants will need to register as a new user. The user name and password you create will be required to access your application status and to apply for additional jobs. Current FAU Employees Current FAU Employees must apply by logging in to Workday . Current FAU employees must apply as an internal applicant by logging into their existing Workday employee account. Executive Searches For executive-level positions managed by external search firms, please visit our Executive Searches page . Applicant Tutorial and Information The Special Instructions to Applicant is located at the bottom of each job vacancy announcement. This section includes important instructions such as required documents, pre-employment screenings, deadlines, etc. Applicants should read the Special Instructions to Applicants before applying. Applicants who submit an incomplete application may not be considered for employment. For instructions on how to apply through our new applicant portal, please review the applicable tutorial instructions . Each tutorial provides step-by-step instructions on how to successfully submit an application. If you have any questions regarding the application process, please email jobs@fau.edu or 561-297-3057. If you require an accommodation to participate in any part of the recruitment process, please contact Florida Atlantic’s Office of Civil Rights and Title IX at 561-297-3004 or send an email to accomodate@fau.edu . For communications assistance, call 7-1-1. Consumer Information Visit Florida Atlantic's Consumer Information webpage for more information about financial aid, its campus, facilities, student athletes, campus security, fire safety, as well as preventing drug and alcohol abuse. Paper copies are available upon request by contacting the Office of Student Financial Aid . Florida Atlantic University 777 Glades Road Boca Raton, FL 33431 Campuses Boca Raton Dania Beach Davie Fort Lauderdale Harbor Branch Jupiter Resources Academic Calendar Employment Opportunities Program Search Parking Report a Concern Transcripts Info Contact Us Directory Emergency & Safety FAU Schools Media Social facebook twitter youtube instagram linkedin Search Programs Request Info Visit Our Campuses If you are experiencing difficulty accessing information on the Florida Atlantic University website due to a disability, visit the website accessibility page. Florida Atlantic University embodies a culture of strategic and collaborative community engagement that results in mutual benefit to the institution and the internal and external communities that it serves. Privacy Policy Regulations & Policies Consumer Information Get Help Site Index Student Accessibility Public Records 2026 Florida Atlantic University ©"
    },
    "https://a.cms.omniupdate.com/11/?skin=fau&account=chordata&site=Primary&action=de&path=/jobs/index.pcf": {
